  "why": "A long flatbed truck on an open road, seen from a little above so every wheel's angle reads: its tail swings into a post, then a motor and rod steer the rear wheels, first against the front (it pivots tight), then the same way (it tracks straight). Close high shots on the axles for each wheel change, the whole truck for each swing.",
  "story": {
   "title": "How Four-Wheel Steering Turns a Giant Truck Like a Compact",
   "hero": "four-wheel steering",
   "parts": [
