  },
  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you only steer the front wheels of a long truck, you have a wide turn."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But the long body cannot pivot, so its tail swings out wide toward a post."
   },
   {
    "role": "stakes",
    "text": "The swinging tail clips the post and knocks it flat, and in a tight street that means a crunched bumper."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So you bolt a steering motor and a rod onto the rear axle, so the back wheels can turn too."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is four-wheel steering."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "At a crawl, the motor turns the rear wheels against the front ones, and the truck pivots in a tight circle."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "A Mercedes S-Class turns its rear wheels up to 10 degrees and cuts its turning circle by up to about 2 meters."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But now at highway speed, rear wheels turned against the front make the tail whip around."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "So above about 37 miles per hour, the rear wheels turn the same way as the front, and the truck tracks straight."
   },
   {
    "role": "name2",
    "text": "Turning the same way is called in-phase steering, and the tight low-speed turn is called counter-phase."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But now if the motor fails, the rod snaps, the rear wheels stick, and the truck veers."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you add a spring that pulls the rear wheels back to center and holds them straight."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add headlights and side mirrors, and the truck is ready for tight streets."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built a truck that turns like a compact car."
   }
  ],
